 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "A finite type ideal is compact in the lattice of quasi-coherent ideals",
 "statement": "Let $X$ be quasi-compact, let $\\mathcal A\\subseteq\\mathcal O_X$ be a finite\ntype quasi-coherent ideal, and let $(\\mathcal B_\\alpha)_\\alpha$ be a nonempty\nfamily of quasi-coherent ideals on $X$ which is directed under inclusion. If\n$\\mathcal A\\subseteq\\bigcup_\\alpha\\mathcal B_\\alpha$, then\n$\\mathcal A\\subseteq\\mathcal B_{\\alpha_0}$ for some single index $\\alpha_0$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-thm-nagata-sketch-conrad/lemma-nagata-finite-type-ideal-compact.md",
  "place": "node lemma-nagata-finite-type-ideal-compact, order 204"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "On an affine open $\\operatorname{Spec}(R)$ the assertion is that a finitely\ngenerated ideal of $R$ contained in the union of a directed family of ideals\nis already contained in one member: each of the finitely many generators lies\nin some member, and directedness produces a member above all of them. Since\n$X$ is quasi-compact it is covered by finitely many affine opens, and\ndirectedness once more produces a single index above the finitely many\nindices obtained on the members of the cover. Containment of quasi-coherent\nideals may be checked on an affine cover, so that index works.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  }
 ],
